ls:\n   - Alleviate symptoms\n   - Prevent complications\n   - Prevent transmission to others\n\n3. Medication Recommendations:\n   - Acetaminophen (Tylenol) 500-1000 mg every 4-6 hours as needed for fever. Do not exceed 4000 mg in 24 hours.\n   - Ibuprofen (Advil) 200-400 mg every 4-6 hours as needed for fever. Do not exceed 1200 mg in 24 hours.\n   - Note: These are over-the-counter medications. If symptoms persist or worsen, the patient should seek medical attention.\n\n4. Non-Pharmacological Interventions:\n   - Rest and hydration\n   - Isolation to prevent transmission to others\n   - Use of a humidifier to soothe a sore throat or cough if present\n\n5. Follow-Up Schedule:\n   - If symptoms persist or worsen after 3-5 days, the patient should seek medical attention.\n\n6. Monitoring Parameters:\n   - Monitor temperature regularly\n   - Monitor for the development of any new symptoms\n\n7. Patient Education Points:\n   - Importance of hand hygiene to prevent transmission\n   - Importance of rest and hydration\n   - When to seek medical attention (persistent or worsening symptoms)\n\n8. Potential Complications to Watch For:\n   - High fever (>103°F or 39.4°C)\n   - Fever lasting more than a week\n   - Severe headache\n   - Shortness of breath\n   - Chest pain\n   - Abdominal pain\n   - Rash\n   - Neck stiffness\n   - Confusion or altered mental status\n   - Any other severe or worsening symptoms\n\nPlease note that this treatment plan is based on the limited information provided and should not replace a comprehensive evaluation by a healthcare professional. The patient should be advised to seek medical attention for proper diagnosis and treatment.', 'Medications:\n1. Acetaminophen (Tylenol) - 500-1000 mg - Every 4-6 hours as needed for fever - Do not exceed 4000 mg in 24 hours\n2. Ibuprofen (Advil) - 200-400 mg - Every 4-6 hours as needed for fever - Do not exceed 1200 mg in 24 hours\n\nInstructions:\n- Take the medication as needed for fever\n- Monitor your temperature regularly\n- Rest and stay hydrated\n- Isolate yourself to prevent transmission to others\n- Use a humidifier to soothe a sore throat or cough if present\n- Seek medical attention if symptoms persist or worsen after 3-5 days\n\nPrecautions:\n- Do not exceed the recommended daily dosage for each medication\n- Wash your hands regularly to prevent transmission\n- Monitor for the development of any new symptoms\n- Seek immediate medical attention if you experience high fever (>103°F or 39.4°C), fever lasting more than a week, severe headache, shortness of breath, chest pain, abdominal pain, rash, neck stiffness, confusion or altered mental status, or any other severe or worsening symptoms.', 992, 992, '2025-10-09 22:02:25', '2025-10-09 22:04:12', 98),
