   - Viral Infection (specific virus not identified)\n\n2. Treatment Goals:\n   - Alleviate symptoms\n   - Prevent complications\n   - Prevent transmission to others\n\n3. Medication Recommendations:\n   - Acetaminophen 500mg every 4-6 hours as needed for fever (not to exceed 3000mg in 24 hours)\n   - Note: Antiviral medication may be considered if a specific virus is identified and if it is within the treatment window.\n\n4. Non-Pharmacological Interventions:\n   - Rest and hydration\n   - Isolation to prevent transmission to others until fever has resolved for at least 24 hours without the use of fever-reducing medications\n\n5. Follow-Up Schedule:\n   - Follow-up in 3-5 days if symptoms persist or worsen\n   - Immediate medical attention if severe symptoms develop (e.g., difficulty breathing, chest pain, severe weakness)\n\n6. Monitoring Parameters:\n   - Monitor temperature daily\n   - Monitor for development of new symptoms or worsening of existing symptoms\n\n7. Patient Education Points:\n   - Importance of hand hygiene and respiratory etiquette to prevent transmission\n   - Importance of adequate rest and hydration\n   - Understanding when to seek medical attention (e.g., severe symptoms, symptoms lasting more than a week)\n\n8. Potential Complications to Watch For:\n   - Dehydration due to fever\n   - Progression of viral infection leading to more severe illness (e.g., pneumonia)\n   - Transmission to others, particularly those who are vulnerable (e.g., elderly, immunocompromised)\n\nPlease note that this treatment plan is based on the assumption of a viral infection. If symptoms persist or worsen, further diagnostic testing may be necessary to identify the specific cause of the fever. Always consult with a healthcare professional for proper diagnosis and treatment.', 'Medications:\n1. Acetaminophen - 500mg - Every 4-6 hours as needed for fever - Until symptoms subside (not to exceed 3000mg in 24 hours)\n\nInstructions:\n- Take the medication with a full glass of water.\n- Do not take more than the recommended dose.\n- Rest and stay hydrated.\n- Isolate yourself to prevent transmission to others until fever has resolved for at least 24 hours without the use of fever-reducing medications.\n\nPrecautions:\n- Monitor your temperature daily.\n- Seek immediate medical attention if severe symptoms develop (e.g., difficulty breathing, chest pain, severe weakness).\n- Follow-up in 3-5 days if symptoms persist or worsen.\n- Practice good hand hygiene and respiratory etiquette to prevent transmission.\n- Be aware of the potential for dehydration due to fever and progression of viral infection leading to more severe illness (e.g., pneumonia).\n- Be mindful of the risk of transmission to others, particularly those who are vulnerable (e.g., elderly, immunocompromised).', 992, 992, '2025-10-09 22:22:37', '2025-10-09 22:28:19', 98),
