 Alleviate symptoms\n   - Prevent complications\n   - Prevent transmission to others\n\n3. Medication Recommendations:\n   - Acetaminophen (Tylenol) 500 mg every 4-6 hours as needed for fever. Do not exceed 3000 mg in 24 hours.\n   - Ibuprofen (Advil) 200-400 mg every 4-6 hours as needed for fever. Do not exceed 1200 mg in 24 hours.\n   - Note: These are over-the-counter medications. If symptoms persist or worsen, the patient should consult a healthcare professional.\n\n4. Non-Pharmacological Interventions:\n   - Rest and hydration\n   - Isolation to prevent transmission to others\n   - Balanced diet to support immune system\n\n5. Follow-Up Schedule:\n   - If symptoms persist or worsen after 3-5 days, the patient should seek medical attention.\n\n6. Monitoring Parameters:\n   - Monitor temperature regularly\n   - Monitor for worsening symptoms or the development of new symptoms\n\n7. Patient Education Points:\n   - Understand the nature of viral infections and their self-limiting course\n   - Understand the importance of rest, hydration, and nutrition in recovery\n   - Understand the importance of preventing transmission to others\n\n8. Potential Complications to Watch For:\n   - High fever (>103°F or 39.4°C)\n   - Fever lasting more than a week\n   - Severe headache\n   - Shortness of breath\n   - Chest pain\n   - Abdominal pain\n   - Confusion or altered mental status\n   - Rash or other skin changes\n   - Any other severe or worsening symptoms\n\nPlease note that this treatment plan is based on the limited information provided and may not cover all possible conditions or complications. It is recommended that the patient consult with a healthcare professional for a proper diagnosis and treatment.', 'Medications:\n1. Acetaminophen (Tylenol) - 500 mg - Every 4-6 hours as needed for fever - Do not exceed 3000 mg in 24 hours\n2. Ibuprofen (Advil) - 200-400 mg - Every 4-6 hours as needed for fever - Do not exceed 1200 mg in 24 hours\n\nInstructions:\n- Take the medication as needed for fever. Do not exceed the maximum daily dosage.\n- Monitor your temperature regularly.\n- If symptoms persist or worsen after 3-5 days, seek medical attention.\n- Rest and stay hydrated.\n- Maintain a balanced diet to support your immune system.\n- Isolate yourself to prevent transmission to others.\n\nPrecautions:\n- Do not take both Acetaminophen and Ibuprofen at the same time. Wait at least 4 hours between taking these medications.\n- If you experience any of the following, seek immediate medical attention: high fever (>103°F or 39.4°C), fever lasting more than a week, severe headache, shortness of breath, chest pain, abdominal pain, confusion or altered mental status, rash or other skin changes, or any other severe or worsening symptoms.\n- These are over-the-counter medications. If symptoms persist or worsen, consult a healthcare professional.', 992, 992, '2025-10-09 22:30:47', '2025-10-09 22:31:29', 98),
